 "notes": "Build diagnostics, seed 0, from a one-off script (not RESULT lines). Week 1 vs week 2 domain AUC: 0.6076 at 200,000 trips per side and 0.6105 on all rows, so the break AUC is not a sample-size effect; without the two Mondays (1 and 8 January) it is 0.5958. Week 1 vs week 2 single-feature AUCs: 0.506 to 0.5339 on the ten features, 0.5566 on speed (trip_distance / duration_min, median 0.172 vs 0.159 miles per minute) and 0.5614 on trip_distance plus duration_min together; dropping any one feature lowers the AUC by at most 0.019 (hour). January vs July single-feature AUCs top out at 0.549 (fare_amount). passenger_count is missing on 0.0473 of January trips and 0.0907 of July trips (the payment_type 0 rows); KS and PSI drop missing values, the classifier sees them. Forecaster: 59 zones; mean pickups per zone-hour 70.07 in January week 4 and 72.1 in July week 2; seasonal-naive MAE (lag_168 alone) 14.371 vs 24.415, last-hour naive MAE (lag_1 alone) 17.87 vs 17.928. July week 1 (1 to 7 July) holds the 4 July holiday, so July week 2's lag_168 reads a holiday week. Derived from the values: the asymptotic KS critical statistic at p = 0.05 is 1.358 x sqrt(1/n1 + 1/n2), which is 0.0043 at 200,000 trips per side and 0.0024 for week 1 vs week 2 (609,698 and 676,839 trips); the forecaster's MAE is 17.6% higher in July week 2 than in January week 4."
